# Weekend Watch — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Every VITE_-prefixed variable is inlined
# into the client bundle at build time, so everything here is PUBLIC by
# definition. Never put a server secret in this file.
#
# The app runs fully without any key: it serves a deterministic offline demo
# catalogue so the UI is exercisable with no credentials and no network.

# --- TMDB credentials (pick ONE; the token is preferred) --------------------

# v4 read access token. Sent as an `Authorization: Bearer` header, which keeps
# the credential out of URLs — and therefore out of browser history, referrer
# headers and server logs.
# Create one at https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
VITE_TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# v3 API key. Sent as a query parameter. Kept for backwards compatibility with
# existing keys; the token above takes precedence when both are set.
VITE_PUBLIC_TMDB_API_KEY=

# --- Overrides (leave unset in normal use) ---------------------------------

# Set to 1 to force the offline demo catalogue even when a key is present.
# Useful for visual regression work and for CI.
# VITE_USE_MOCK_CATALOGUE=1

# TMDB API origin. Only ever overridden in tests.
# VITE_TMDB_BASE_URL=https://api.themoviedb.org/3

# --- Dev / preview servers -------------------------------------------------

# Hostnames the Vite dev and preview servers accept. Vite rejects any request
# whose Host header is not on this list, so set this when developing behind a
# tunnel, a reverse proxy or a cloud sandbox. A leading dot matches all
# subdomains. Comma-separated.
#
#   ALLOWED_HOSTS=.example.com,dev.local
#
# Left unset, any host is accepted, because both servers bind to 0.0.0.0 only so
# a sandboxed preview can reach them. Set this explicitly for any deployment
# reachable from an untrusted network.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=
